# Project principles

- Target a reproducible open-source data platform: local Compose for development/verification and an AWS path as Terraform IaC.
- Prefer simple, modular, reproducible solutions over extra infrastructure.
- Keep business logic out of Airflow DAGs and infrastructure configuration.
- Use environment-specific configuration without duplicating business logic.
- Validate compatibility between storage, table formats, catalogs and query engines before adopting a combination.
- Do not introduce a new technology without stating its purpose and operational cost.
- Do not introduce Kubernetes unless an explicit requirement justifies it.
- Avoid duplicate tools for the same responsibility.
- Work on one issue or one small, coherent task at a time. Do not implement multiple future phases in a single change.
- Prefer an explicit TODO or a documented blocker over speculative implementation.
- Use English for code, identifiers, comments, commit messages and technical documentation. Communicate with the user in Brazilian Portuguese.
- Explain architectural trade-offs clearly. The user makes final architectural decisions.
